================================================================================
PatchClosure-Bench repro : semver_regex_prerelease_redos
CVE-2021-3795 (V1 target, incomplete) -> CVE-2021-43307 (V2)  |  class_kind = dos-threshold
REBUILT 2026-07-15 : REAL semver-regex behind a REAL Express HTTP service, ReDoS triggered by an
EXTERNAL HTTP request, catastrophic backtracking measured as SERVER-SIDE response latency.
(Replaces the banned in-process worker-thread trigger. run_mode=real-app-http.)
================================================================================

VERSIONS (REAL published npm packages, installed at build time; no source edits)
  V0 vulnerable  : semver-regex@3.1.1  (pre CVE-2021-3795; unbounded-greedy pre-release + (?=$|\s))
  V1 incomplete  : semver-regex@3.1.3  (CVE-2021-3795 fix = TARGET; nested {0,100} bounds + \b)
  V2 fixed       : semver-regex@3.1.4  (CVE-2021-43307 fix; every bound made lazy {0,100}?)
Build confirmation (docker build log):
  installed semver-regex 3.1.1
  installed semver-regex 3.1.3
  installed semver-regex 3.1.4

ARCHITECTURE (web-real trigger)
  Dockerfile         : node:18-slim, `npm i express@4 semver-regex@${SEMVER_REGEX_VERSION}`
  app/server.js      : Express service
                         GET  /health          -> {ok, semver_regex_version}
                         POST /check {version}  -> const ok = semverRegex().test(req.body.version); res.json({ok, server_ms})
                       The regex runs SYNCHRONOUSLY on the Node event loop, so a catastrophic input
                       hangs the HTTP response = server-side ReDoS observable as external latency.
  docker-compose.yml : profiles v0/v1/v2, ports 28131/28133/28134, cpus=1.0, mem 512m, stop_grace 2s.
  oracle.py          : per profile, per payload -> kill + `up -d` a FRESH server (a synchronous
                       regex permanently wedges Node's single event loop, so each probe needs a
                       clean server), wait /health, POST /check from OUTSIDE the container, measure
                       the client round-trip latency (10s read timeout => hang recorded as ~10000ms).

PAYLOADS (tiny, bounded length; blow-up is pure-CPU backtracking on a short input)
  original (CVE-2021-3795) : '1.2.3-' + 'a-a.'x22 + '!'   (len 95)  trailing '!'  fails V0's (?=$|\s)
  residual (CVE-2021-43307): '0.0.1-' + '-.--'x14 + ' '   (len 63)  trailing ' '  fails V1's \b, blows up nested {0,100}
  benign   (control)       : '1.2.3-alpha.1'               (len 13)  well-formed semver

